# Machine-specific paths and live toggle state, and the lock and swap file
# that writing it atomically leaves beside it
config.json
config.json.*

# Written here when you install for this repo as the project: the hook config
# and the /voice command, both holding the absolute path to your own python.exe
.claude/

# Engine and hook logs
logs/

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Voices you may keep locally but not publish live outside this repo, via
# "extraVoicesDirs" in config.json. Nothing derived from someone else's
# recording belongs in voices/ -- see VOICES.md.

# Working files from make_pocket_voice.py: the render a voice was cloned from,
# its words, and the same words read back in the clone. A megabyte each,
# regenerable, and only wanted while somebody is comparing the two. The
# pocket.safetensors they produce is the artefact and does belong in the repo.
#
# Breeze is the exception that proves it: it keeps no baked state and learns
# the voice from a clip on every line, so for Breeze the clip *is* the artefact.
# That one is breeze-reference.wav with its .txt, and it is committed.
voices/**/pocket-reference.wav
voices/**/pocket-reference.txt
voices/**/pocket-after.wav

# The retired setup window's build output (setup-app is kept as source only; see its README).
setup-app/bin/
setup-app/obj/
setup-app/dist/

# Voices kept on this machine and never published: the Calradia library carried over from the
# Immersive AI mod lives here. Read through "extraVoicesDirs" in config.json.
voices-local/

# What a pre-2.0 setup.ps1 installed on this machine. Per machine, never published.
installed.json

# The manager agent's working notes (progress, survey) for a multi-step change.
# Scratch for whoever is doing the work, not part of the project.
.manager/
